-- title:
--   Local normalised level transport passes along an isomorphism
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the full Čerednik–Drinfeld rigidification package; the hypotheses are grouped and named below, and every group is accounted for.
--
--   *Base ring data.* Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, a nonzero level $N$ divisible by neither, with $N$ squarefree; a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ which is a domain of characteristic zero with irreducible element $\pi$, residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$, and fraction field $K_0$ of characteristic zero; an $\mathcal O$-algebra `Onr`, a domain of characteristic zero, $\pi$-adically complete, with $(\pi)$ maximal, every element satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ and every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$ (so the residue ring is an algebraic closure of the residue ring of $\mathcal O$), together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $F_r$ congruent to $x \mapsto x^r$ modulo $\pi$; and a homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^n$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   *Moduli data for fake elliptic curves.* An indefinite quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`), and a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal X \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `pt` for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$ (`h𝒳`). An auxiliary level $n \geq 3$ coprime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$, a fine moduli scheme $M \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `ptF` for curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`), a group $G$ acting by automorphisms $\rho$ of $M$ with labels $\chi$ forming a level-twist action (`hρ`), and a morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hp`) invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the point maps (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$ a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ for curves with extra $\ell$-level (`h𝒴`) with the two degeneracy morphisms $d_0, d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realised on points by forgetting the $\ell$-level, respectively by dividing by it (`hd₀`, `hd₁`), and Atkin–Lehner morphisms $a_r$, $a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ realised on points by the corresponding quotients (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   *Definite quaternionic data.* A definite quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`), a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in it, an idele $n_1$ in the $r$-Hecke set of $R_1$ whose intersection order has Eichler level $N r$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$, the place $v$ above $r$, the group $\Gamma^t$ of units integral away from $v$ (`hΓt`), elements $s_\ell$ and $s^f_\ell$ with the local conditions, Hecke conditions and reduced norm $\ell$ collected in `hs`, the groups $\Gamma^t_\ell = \Gamma^t \cap s_\ell \Gamma^t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`), and an element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   *Special fibre data.* The containment $\mathbb Z \subseteq \Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`); an order coordinate system $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{r^2} \times \mathbb Z_{r^2}$ (`hcoord`); a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over the residue ring `Onr`$/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over it (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ realising $A_0$ as the formal module $X_0$ via $\mathrm{coord}$ (`hA₀`); endomorphism families $e, e'$ of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma^t$ with degrees $\deg$, subject to: `hE1` ($e_\gamma, e'_\gamma$ an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg \gamma}$ preserving the level), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity up to $r$-power scalars), `hE1sc` and `hE1'` (rational scalars are detected exactly by scalar $\gamma$), `hE2` (each $e_\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by a central endomorphism whose matrix realisation is $r^{k_\gamma} g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$ for one $g$ independent of $\gamma$), `hE3` (labels in $\Lambda$ for the action of $\Gamma^t$ on a full level-$n$ structure, multiplicative and compatible with scalars modulo $n$), `hE4` (every $r$-power isogeny of a geometric fibre of $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to $r$-power scalars), and an order $R_2 \leq R_1$ with $r$-power denominators together with a family $\hat e$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ satisfying `hE5a`–`hE5e` (additivity on points, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action and preservation of level; unitality, multiplicativity and agreement with the action of integers; the norm relation for $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)$; compatibility with the $e_\gamma$; and a joint matrix realisation for $\Gamma^t$ and $R_2$ simultaneously).
--
--   *The formal-module dictionary.* A ring map $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r^2} \to$ `Onr`, a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over `Onr`$/r$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), a moduli package $MD$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), a classifying map $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $MD$ satisfying `hη` (three clauses: admissible rigidified objects have the same image exactly when isomorphic, naturality under base change, and local liftability of points of $MD$), an injective realisation $E_0$ of the centraliser of $\Phi$ in $M_2(K_0)$ with bounded denominators (`hE₀`), and a comparison $eD$ of the $\mathcal O$-functor attached to $MD$ with the product of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `Onr` and the Deligne-datum functor $\Omega(K_0,\pi)$, natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), with first coordinate the leg (`hfstD`), carrying the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action to the twisted action (`hGLD`), carrying $\pi$-translates to the Frobenius twist of the leg (`hPiD`), and with $\pi$-translates existing (`hPiexD`). A reduction map $\kappa$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`) and an isogeny $\beta_0 : \Phi \to X_0 \otimes \kappa$ of height $4 n_0$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ on the special fibre: $A_{0w}$, $a_w$, $a_w'$, $b_w$, $b_w'$, $k_w$ with `hALw` (Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ via $a_w, a_w'$), `hBSw` (isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$), `hBSwlev` (level preservation) and `hJOINTw` (a joint matrix realisation in which $a_w \circ b_w$ corresponds to $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to an $r$-power).
--
--   *The classifying map $\Xi$.* An assignment $\Xi$ sending a rigidified fake elliptic curve over a Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra to a point of the functor attached to $MD$, subject to `hΞleg` (over a ring with no nontrivial idempotents the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of the given one), `hΞnat` (naturality along base change of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under an isomorphism of curves carrying one rigidification to the other up to $r$-power scalars) and `hΞdef` (an explicit description of $\Xi$ through `IsRigTransport` with $j \leq 1$ and an admissible rigidified object); an element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ` and `heqW` (translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$, respectively by the Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$, corresponds under $\Xi$ to the action of $r^c g_0 \iota_0(\gamma) g_0^{-1}$, respectively $r^c g_0 \iota_0(\bar w) g_0^{-1}$, for some $c \in \mathbb Z$); the four clauses `hK1`–`hK4` comparing $\Xi$ on the $g_0$-twisted leg with the Deligne-datum functor (surjectivity, injectivity up to isomorphism with comparison data, compatibility with base change, and lifting along a surjection with square-zero-like kernel); and finally `hC0e`, `hC0u`: over a Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra with no nontrivial idempotents, a full level-$n$ structure which is the height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification of the $g_0$-twisted leg exists, and any two such agree.
--
--   *The data of the assertion.* A Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi :$ `Onr` $\to B$, fake elliptic curves $E, E'$ over $B$ and an isomorphism $i : E.A \cong E'.A$ over $B$ which is an isomorphism of fake elliptic curves in the sense of `IsoVia`: it transports the group law, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action, and a point factors through the level subscheme of $E$ if and only if its image factors through that of $E'$. Rigidifications $\varrho$ of $E$ and $\varrho'$ of $E'$, both for the leg obtained from $\psi$ by the $(-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0))$-th power of $F_r$; such a rigidification consists of the reduction $E_b$ of the curve modulo $\pi$ together with its comparison morphism, the pull-back $A_b$ of $A_0$ along the residue leg with its morphism to $A_0$, an exponent $d$, and an isogeny pair $\varphi, \varphi'$ of degree $r^d$ from $E_b$ to $A_b$ preserving the level. Comparison data for $i$: a morphism $i_b : \varrho.E_b.A \to \varrho'.E_b.A$ over $B/\pi$ with $i_b$ followed by $\varrho'.g_b$ equal to $\varrho.g_b$ followed by $i$ (`hibg`, `hibf`), a morphism $u_A : \varrho'.A_b.A \to \varrho.A_b.A$ exhibiting $\varrho'.A_b$ as the pull-back of $\varrho.A_b$ along the identity and compatible with the morphisms to $A_0$ (`huA`, `huAg`), and exponents $i_1, j_1$ with the relation `hcorr` stating that $i_b$ followed by $\varrho'.\varphi$, by $u_A$ and by multiplication by $r^{i_1}$ equals $\varrho.\varphi$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j_1}$. Full level-$n$ structures $P_n$ on $E$ and $P_n'$ on $E'$ with $i \circ P_n = P_n'$ (`hPn`).
--
--   *Hypothesis `h`.* For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B_c$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and with no idempotents other than $0$ and $1$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi_c : B \to B_c$, every fake elliptic curve $E_c$ over $B_c$ exhibited as the pull-back of $E$ along $\varphi_c$ by a morphism $g_c$, every rigidification $\varrho_c$ of $E_c$ for the leg $\varphi_c$ composed with the twisted leg which is the pull-back of $\varrho$ along $\varphi_c$, every full level-$n$ structure $P_c$ on $E_c$ whose section composed with $g_c$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\varphi_c)$ followed by the section of $P_n$, and every formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_c$ over $B_c$ with formal coordinates $\theta_c$ realising $E_c$ as $X_c$ via $\mathrm{coord}$: the structure $P_c$ is the height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho_c$, that is, there is a section $Q$ of $\varrho_c.A_b$ over $B_c/\pi$ whose composite with $\varrho_c.g_A$ is the base change of $P_0$ along the residue leg, together with a formal module $X$, formal coordinates $\theta$ realising $E_c$ via $\mathrm{coord}$, an index $j \leq 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ over $B_c$ with $t.X = X$, satisfying `IsRigTransport` for $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$, $\varrho_c$, $\theta$, $j$, admissible for $\iota$ and the $(-j)$-fold Frobenius twist of the leg, and such that the reduction modulo $\pi$ of $r^{t.n}$ times $P_c$ equals $Q$ followed by $\varrho_c.\varphi'$ and $\varrho_c.g_b$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* The same property holds for the primed data: for every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B_c$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and no nontrivial idempotents, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi_c : B \to B_c$, every fake elliptic curve $E_c$ over $B_c$ exhibited as the pull-back of $E'$ along $\varphi_c$ by a morphism $g_c$, every rigidification $\varrho_c$ of $E_c$ for the leg $\varphi_c$ composed with the twisted leg which is the pull-back of $\varrho'$ along $\varphi_c$, every full level-$n$ structure $P_c$ on $E_c$ whose section composed with $g_c$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\varphi_c)$ followed by the section of $P_n'$, and every formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_c$ with formal coordinates $\theta_c$ realising $E_c$ via $\mathrm{coord}$: the structure $P_c$ is the height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho_c$, in the sense just unfolded.
--
--   This is the isomorphism-invariance step in the rigidification layer of the Čerednik–Drinfeld dictionary for fake elliptic curves: the property of being, after every connected test base change, the height-normalised transport of the fixed level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on the special fibre is carried along an isomorphism of fake elliptic curves together with the matching comparison data between their rigidifications. It is used in the construction of the $p$-adic uniformisation family on the fine moduli scheme and on the Hecke tower, and in the local lifting of values of that family over square-zero extensions.
